      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The primary criticisms against high-density zoning often revolve around the perceived destruction of neighborhood character and the strain on existing infrastructure. Opponents frequently argue that increased density leads to overcrowding, traffic congestion, and a loss of community feel. Furthermore, there is a persistent fear that these projects will negatively impact property values for current residents.",
